6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
7. Switch legs and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/One_Leg_Barbell_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Open Palm Kettlebell Clean', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place one kettlebell between vos pieds. Clean the kettlebell by extending through the legs and hanches as you raise the kettlebell towards your épaules.
2. Release the kettlebell as it comes up, and let it flip so that the ball of the kettlebell lands in the palms of vos mains.
3. Release the kettlebell out in front of you and catch the handle with both hands. Lower the kettlebell to the position de départ and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Open_Palm_Kettlebell_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Otis-Up', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Secure vos pieds and lay back on le sol. Your genous should be bent. Hold a poids with both hands to your poitrine. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Initiate le mouvement by flexing the hanches and spine to raise your torse up from the ground.
3. As you move up, press the poids up so that it is above votre tête at the top of le mouvement.
4. Return the poids to your poitrine as you reverse the sit-up motion, ensuring not to go all the way down to le sol.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Otis-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Overhead Cable Curl', 'Biceps', 'Poulie', '1. To begin, set a poids that is comfortable on each side of the pulley machine. Note: Make sure that the amount of poids selected is the same on each side.
2. Now adjust the height of the pulleys on each side and make sure that they are positioned at a height higher than that of your épaules.
3. Stand in the middle of both sides and use an prise en supination (paumes vers towards the ceiling) to grab each handle. vos bras should be fully extended and parallèle au sol with vos pieds positioned épaule width apart from each other. votre corps should be evenly aligned the handles. C''est votre position de départ.
4. While exhaling, Lentement, squeeze the biceps on each side until your forearms and biceps touch.
5. While inhaling, move your forearms back to the position de départ. Note: Your entire body is stationary during cet exercice except for the forearms.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. prescribed in your program.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Overhead_Cable_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Overhead Lat', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Sit upright on le sol with your partner behind you. Raise one arm straight up, and flex the coude, attempting to touch your hand to votre dos. Your parner should hold your triceps and poignet. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Attempt to pull your upper arm to your side as your partner prevents you from doing actually doing so.
3. After 10-20 seconds, relax the arm and allow your partner to further stretch the lat by applying gentle pressure to the triceps. Maintenez 10-20 secondes, and then switch sides.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Overhead_Lat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Overhead Slam', 'Dos', 'Medecine ball', '1. Hold a medine ball with both hands and Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds at épaule width. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Initiate the countermovement by raising the ball above votre tête and fully extending votre corps.
3. Reverse the motion, slamming the ball into the ground directly in front of you as hard as you can.
4. Receive the ball with both hands on the bounce and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Overhead_Slam/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Overhead Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Start out by having a barre in front of you on le sol. vos pieds should be wider than épaule width apart from each other.
2. Bend the genous and use a pronated grip (paumes vers you) to grab the barre. vos mains should be at a wider than épaule width apart from each other before lifting. Once you are positioned, lift the barre up until you can rest it on your poitrine.
3. Move the barre over and slightly behind votre tête and make sure vos bras are fully extended. Keep votre tête up en permanence and also maintain a straight back. Retract your omoplates. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Lentement, lower the poids by bending your genous until your cuisses are parallel to the ground while inhaling. Conseil : Keep votre dos straight while performing cet exercice to avoid any injuries and vos bras should remain extended and over votre tête en permanence.
5. Now use vos pieds and legs to help bring the poids back up to the position de départ while exhaling.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Overhead_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Overhead Stretch', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Standing straight up, lace your fingers together and open your palms to the ceiling. Keep your épaules down as you extend vos bras up.
2. To create a full torse stretch, pull your tailbone down and stabilize your torse as you do this. Stretch the muscles on both the front and the back of the torse.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Avant-bras, Dos, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Overhead_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Overhead Triceps', 'Triceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Sit upright on le sol with your partner behind you. Raise one arm straight up, and flex the coude, attempting to touch your hand to votre dos. Your parner should hold your coude and poignet. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Attempt to extend the arm straight into the air as your partner prevents you from doing actually doing so.
3. After 10-20 seconds, relax the arm and allow your partner to further stretch the triceps by applying gentle pressure to the poignet. Maintenez 10-20 secondes, and then switch sides.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Overhead_Triceps/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Pallof Press', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect a standard handle to a tower, and—if possible—position the cable to épaule height. If not, a low pulley will suffice.
2. With your side to the cable, grab the handle with both hands and step away from the tower. You should be approximately arm''s length away from the pulley, with the tension of the poids on the cable.
3. With vos pieds positioned hanche-width apart and genous slightly bent, hold the cable to the middle of your poitrine. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Press the cable away from your poitrine, fully extending both arms. You sangle abdominale should be tight and engaged.
5. Hold the repetition for several seconds before returning to the position de départ.
6. At the conclusion of the set, Répétez facing the other direction.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Pallof_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Pallof Press With Rotation', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect a standard handle to a tower, and position the cable to épaule height.
2. With your side to the cable, grab the handle with one hand and step away from the tower. You should be approximately arm''s length away from the pulley, with the tension of the poids on the cable. Align outstretched arm with cable.
3. With vos pieds positioned hanche-width apart, pull the cable into your poitrine and grab the handle with your other hand. Both hands should be on the handle at this time.
4. Facing forward, press the cable away from your poitrine. You sangle abdominale should be tight and engaged.
5. Keeping your hanches straight, twist your torse away from the pulley until you get a full quarter rotation.
6. Maintain your rigid stance and straight arms. Return to the neutral position in a slow and controlled manner. vos bras should be extended in front of you.
7. With the side tension still engaging your sangle abdominale, bring vos mains to your poitrine and immediately press outward to a fully extended position. This constitutes one rep.
8. Répétez to failure.
9. Then, reposition and Répétez the same series of movements on the opposite side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Pallof_Press_With_Rotation/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Palms-Down Dumbbell Wrist Curl Over A Bench', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Start out by placing two haltères on one side of a flat banc.
2. Kneel down on both of your genous so that votre corps is facing the flat banc.
3. Use vos bras to grab both of the haltères with a pronated grip (paumes vers down) and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against the flat banc. Your poignets should be hanging over the edge.
4. Start out by curling your poignet upwards and exhaling.
5. Lentement, lower your poignets back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
6. Your forearms should be stationary as your poignet is the only movement needed to perform cet exercice.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Palms-Down_Dumbbell_Wrist_Curl_Over_A_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Palms-Down Wrist Curl Over A Bench', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Start out by placing a barre on one side of a flat banc.
2. Kneel down on both of your genous so that votre corps is facing the flat banc.
3. Use vos bras to grab the barre with a pronated grip (palms down) and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against the flat banc. Your poignets should be hanging over the edge.
4. Start out by curling your poignet upwards and exhaling.
5. Lentement, lower your poignets back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
6. Your forearms should be stationary as your poignet is the only movement needed to perform cet exercice.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Palms-Down_Wrist_Curl_Over_A_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Palms-Up Barbell Wrist Curl Over A Bench', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Start out by placing a barre on one side of a flat banc.
2. Kneel down on both of your genous so that votre corps is facing the flat banc.
3. Use vos bras to grab the barre with a supinated grip (palms up) and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against the flat banc. Your poignets should be hanging over the edge.
4. Start out by curling your poignet upwards and exhaling.
5. Lentement, lower your poignets back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
6. Your forearms should be stationary as your poignet is the only movement needed to perform cet exercice.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Palms-Up_Barbell_Wrist_Curl_Over_A_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Palms-Up Dumbbell Wrist Curl Over A Bench', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Start out by placing two haltères on one side of a flat banc.
2. Kneel down on both of your genous so that votre corps is facing the flat banc.
3. Use vos bras to grab both of the haltères with a supinated grip (palms up) and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against the flat banc. Your poignets should be hanging over the edge.
4. Start out by curling your poignet upwards and exhaling.
5. Lentement, lower your poignets back down to the position de départ while inhaling. Make sure to inspirez during this part of the exercise.
6. Your forearms should be stationary as your poignet is the only movement needed to perform cet exercice.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Palms-Up_Dumbbell_Wrist_Curl_Over_A_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Parallel Bar Dip', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. Stand between a set of parallel bars. Place a hand on each bar, and then take a small jump to help you get into the position de départ with vos bras locked out.
2. Begin by flexing the coude, lowering votre corps until vos bras break 90 degrees. Avoid swinging, and maintain good posture throughout the descent.
3. Reverse the motion by extending the coude, pushing yourself back up into the position de départ.
4. Répétez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Parallel_Bar_Dip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Pelvic Tilt Into Bridge', 'Bas du dos', 'Autre', '1. Lie down with vos pieds on le sol, heels directly under your genous.
2. Lift only your tailbone to the ceiling to stretch your lower back. (Don''t lift the entire spine yet.) Pull in your stomach.
3. To go into a bridge, lift the entire spine except the neck.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Pelvic_Tilt_Into_Bridge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Peroneals-SMR', 'Mollets', 'Foam roller', '1. Lay on your side, supporting your poids on your forearm and on a foam roller placed on the outside of your lower leg. Your upper leg can either be on top of your lower leg, or you can cross it in front of you. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Raise your hanches off of the ground and begin to roll from below the genou to above the cheville on the side of your leg, pausing at points of tension for 10-30 seconds. Répétez de l''autre côté.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Peroneals-SMR/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Peroneals Stretch', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. In a seated position, loop a belt, rope, or band around one foot. C''est votre position de départ.
2. With the leg extended and the heel off of the ground, pull on the belt so that the foot is inverted, with the inside of the foot being pulled towards you. Maintenez 10-20 secondes, and then switch sides.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Peroneals_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Physioball Hip Bridge', 'Fessiers', 'Swiss ball', '1. Lay on a ball so that your upper back is on the ball with your hanches unsupported. Both feet should be flat on le sol, hanche width apart or wider. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by extending the hanches using your fessiers and ischio-jambiers, raising your hanches upward as you bridge.
3. Pause at the top of the motion and Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Physioball_Hip_Bridge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Pin Presses', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Pin presses remove the eccentric phase of the banc press, developing starting strength. They also allow you to train a desired range of motion.
2. The banc should be set up in a power rack. Set the pins to the desired point in your range of motion, whether it just be lockout or an inch off of your poitrine. The bar should be moved to the pins and prepared for lifting.
3. Begin by lying on the banc, with the bar directly above the contact point during your regular banc. Tuck vos pieds underneath you and arch votre dos. Using the bar to help support your poids, lift your épaule off the banc and retract them, squeezing the omoplates together. Use vos pieds to drive your traps into the banc. Maintain this tight body position throughout le mouvement.
4. You can take a standard banc grip, or épaule width to focus on the triceps. The bar, poignet, and coude should stay in line en permanence. Focus on squeezing the bar and trying to pull it apart.
5. Drive the bar up with as much force as possible. The coudes should be tucked in until lockout.
6. Return the bar to the pins, pausing before beginning the next repetition.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Avant-bras, Dos, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Pin_Presses/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Piriformis-SMR', 'Fessiers', 'Foam roller', '1. Sit with your buttocks on top of a foam roll. Bend your genous, and then cross one leg so that the cheville is over the genou. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Shift your poids to the side of the crossed leg, rolling over the buttocks until you feel tension in your upper fessiers. You may assist the stretch by using one hand to pull the bent genou towards your poitrine. Hold this position for 10-30 seconds, and then switch sides.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Piriformis-SMR/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Plank', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Get into a prone position on le sol, supporting your poids on your toes and your forearms. vos bras are bent and directly below the épaule.
2. Keep votre corps straight en permanence, and hold this position as long as possible. To increase difficulty, an arm or leg can be raised.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Plank/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Plate Pinch', 'Avant-bras', 'Autre', '1. Grab two wide-rimmed plates and put them together with the smooth sides facing outward
2. Use your fingers to grip the outside part of the plate and your thumb for the other side thus holding both plates together. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Squeeze the plate with your fingers and thumb. Hold this position for as long as you can.
4. Répétez for the recommended amount of sets prescribed in your program.
5. Switch arms and Répétez le mouvements.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Plate_Pinch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Plate Twist', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol or an exercise mat with vos jambes fully extended and your upper body upright. Grab the plate by its sides with both hands out in front of your abdominals with vos bras slightly bent.
2. Lentement, cross vos jambes near your chevilles and lift them up off the ground. Your genous should also be bent slightly. Note: Move your upper body back slightly to help keep you balanced turning cet exercice. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Move the plate to the left side and touch le sol with it. Expirez as you perform that movement.
4. Come back to the position de départ as you Inspirez and then Répétez le mouvement but this time to the right side of the body. Conseil : Use a slow controlled movement en permanence. Jerking motions can injure the back.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Plate_Twist/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Platform Hamstring Slides', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. For this movement a wooden floor or similar is needed. Lay on votre dos with vos jambes extended. Place a gym towel or a light poids underneath your heel. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin le mouvement by flexing the genou, keeping your other leg straight.
3. Continue bringing the heel closer to you, sliding it on le sol.
4. At full genou flexion, reverse le mouvement to Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Platform_Hamstring_Slides/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Plie Dumbbell Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Haltères', '1. Hold a haltère at the base with both hands and stand straight up. Move vos jambes so that they are wider than épaule width apart from each other with your genous slightly bent.
2. Your toes should be facing out. Note: vos bras should be stationary while performing the exercise. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lentement, bend the genous and lower vos jambes until your cuisses are parallèle au sol. Make sure to inspirez as this is the eccentric part of the exercise.
4. Press mainly with the heel of the foot to bring the body back to the position de départ while exhaling.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Plie_Dumbbell_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Plyo Kettlebell Pushups', 'Pectoraux', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place a kettlebell on le sol. Place yourself in a pushup position, on your toes with one hand on the ground and one hand holding the kettlebell, with your coudes extended. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by lowering yourself as low as you can, keeping votre dos straight.
3. Quickly and forcefully reverse direction, pushing yourself up to the other side of the kettlebell, switching hands as you do so. Continue le mouvement by descending and Répétezing le mouvement back and forth.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Plyo_Kettlebell_Pushups/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Plyo Push-up', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Move into a prone position on le sol, supporting your poids on vos mains and toes.
2. vos bras should be fully extended with the hands around épaule width. Keep votre corps straight throughout le mouvement. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Descend by flexing at the coude, lowering your poitrine towards the ground.
4. At the bottom, reverse the motion by pushing yourself up through coude extension as quickly as possible. Attempt to push your upper body up until vos mains leave the ground.
5. Revenez en position de départ and Répétez the exercise.
6. For added difficulty, add claps into le mouvement while you are air borne.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Plyo_Push-up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Posterior Tibialis Stretch', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. In a seated position, loop a belt, rope, or band around one foot. C''est votre position de départ.
2. With the leg extended and the heel off of the ground, pull on the belt so that the foot is everted, with the outside of the foot being pulled towards you. Maintenez 10-20 secondes, and then switch sides.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Posterior_Tibialis_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Power Clean', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds slightly wider than épaule width apart and toes pointing out slightly.
2. Squat down and grasp bar with a closed, pronated grip. vos mains should be slightly wider than épaule width apart outside genous with coudes fully extended.
3. Place the bar about 1 inch in front of your shins and over the balls of vos pieds.
4. votre dos should be flat or slightly arched, your poitrine held up and out and your omoplates should be retracted.
5. Keep votre tête in a neutral position (in line with vertebral column and not tilted or rotated) with your eyes focused straight ahead. Inspirez during this phase.
6. Lift the bar from le sol by forcefully extending the hanches and the genous as you expirez. Conseil : The upper torse should maintain the same angle. Do not bend at the waist yet and do not let the hanches rise before the épaules (this would have the effect of pushing the fessiers in the air and stretching the ischio-jambiers.
7. Keep coudes fully extended with the head in a neutral position and the épaules over the bar.
8. As the bar raises keep it as close to the shins as possible.
9. As the bar passes the genous, thrust your hanches forward and slightly bend the genous to avoid locking them. Conseil : At this point your cuisses should be against the bar.
10. Keep the back flat or slightly arched, coudes fully extended and votre tête neutral. Conseil : You will hold your breath until the next phase.
11. Inspirez and then forcefully and quickly extend your hanches and genous and stand on your toes.
12. Keep the bar as close to votre corps as possible. Conseil : votre dos should be flat with the coudes pointed out to the sides and votre tête in a neutral position. Also, keep your épaules over the bar and arms straight as long as possible.
13. When your lower body joints are fully extended, shrug the épaules upward rapidly without letting the coudes flex yet. Expirez during this portion of le mouvement.
14. As the épaules reach their highest elevation flex your coudes to begin pulling votre corps under the bar.
15. Continue to pull the arms as high and as long as possible. Conseil : Due to the explosive nature of this phase, your torse will be erect or with an arched back, votre tête will be tilted back slightly and vos pieds may lose contact with le sol.
16. After the lower body has fully extended and the bar reaches near maximal height, pull votre corps under the bar and rotate the arms around and under the bar.
17. Simultaneously, flex the hanches and genous into a quarter squat position.
18. Once the arms are under the bar, inspirez and then lift your coudes to position the upper arms parallèle au sol. Rack the bar across the front of your collar bones and front épaule muscles.
19. Catch the bar with an erect and tight torse, a neutral head position and flat feet. Expirez during this movement.
20. Levez-vous by extending the hanches and genous to a fully erect position.
21. Lower the bar by gradually reducing the muscular tension of the arms to allow a controlled descent of the bar to the cuisses. Inspirez during this movement.
22. Simultaneously flex the hanches and genous to cushion the impact of the bar on the cuisses.
23. Squat down with the coudes fully extended until the bar touches le sol.
24. Start over at Phase 1 and Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Power_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Power Clean from Blocks', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. With a barre on boxes of the desired height, take a grip just outside the legs. Lower your hanches with the poids focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, poitrine up, with your épaules just in front of the bar. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your genous. votre dos angle should stay the same, and vos bras should remain straight. As the bar approaches the mid-cuisse position, begin extending through the hanches.
3. In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hanches, genous, and chevilles, using speed to move the bar upward. There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the poids. At the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back, with the arms still extended.
4. As full extension is achieved, transition into the third pull by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the coudes up and out. At peak extension, pull yourself under the bar far enough that it can be racked onto the épaules, rotating your coudes under the bar as you do so. The bar should be racked onto the protracted épaules, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed.
5. Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torse upright and coudes up. Continue until you have risen to a standing position, and complete the repetition by returning the poids to the boxes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Quadriceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Power_Clean_from_Blocks/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Power Jerk', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Standing with the poids racked on the front of the épaules, begin with the dip. With vos pieds directly under your hanches, flex the genous without moving the hanches backward. Go down only slightly, and reverse direction as powerfully as possible.
2. Drive through the heels create as much speed and force as possible, and be sure to move votre tête out of the way as the bar leaves the épaules.
3. At this moment as the feet leave le sol, the feet must be placed into the receiving position as quickly as possible. In the brief moment the feet are not actively driving against the platform, the athletes effort to push the bar up will drive them down. The feet should be moved to a slightly wider stance, with the genous partially bent.
4. Receive the bar with the arms locked out overhead.
5. Return to a standing position.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Power_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Power Partials', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright and a haltère on each hand being held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse.
2. The palms of the hands should be facing your torse. vos pieds should be about épaule width apart. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping vos bras straight and the torse stationary, lift the poids out to your sides until they are about épaule level height while exhaling.
4. Feel the contraction for a second and begin to lower the poids back down to the position de départ while inhaling. Conseil : Keep the paumes vers down with the little finger slightly higher while lifting and lowering the poids as it will concentrate the stress on your épaules mainly.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Power_Partials/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Power Snatch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a loaded barre on le sol. The bar should be close to or touching the shins, and a prise large should be taken on the bar. The feet should be directly below the hanches, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hanches, with the poitrine up and the head looking forward. The épaules should be just in front of the bar. This will be the position de départ.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar from the ground. The back angle should stay the same until the bar passes the genous.
3. Transition into the second pull by extending through the hanches genous and chevilles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body. At peak extension, shrug the épaules and allow the coudes to flex to the side.
4. As you move vos pieds into the receiving position, a slightly wider position, pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. The bar should be received in a partial squat. Continue raising the bar to the overhead position, receiving the bar locked out overhead.
5. Return to a standing position with the poids over head.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Power_Snatch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Power Snatch from Blocks', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a loaded barre on boxes or stands of the desired height. A prise large should be taken on the bar. The feet should be directly below the hanches, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hanches, with the poitrine up and the head looking forward. The épaules should be just in front of the bar, with the coudes pointed out. This will be the position de départ.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar from the boxes.
3. Transition into the second pull by extending through the hanches genous and chevilles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body. At peak extension, shrug the épaules and allow the coudes to flex to the side.
4. As you move vos pieds into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. The feet should move to just outside the hanches, turned out as necessary. Receive the bar above a full squat and with the arms fully extended overhead.
5. Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, votre tête and poitrine up, drive through heels of the feet to move to a standing position. Carefully return the poids to the boxes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Power_Snatch_from_Blocks/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Power Stairs', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. In the power stairs, implements are moved up a staircase. For training purposes, these can be performed with a tire or box.
2. Begin by taking the implement with both hands. Set vos pieds wide, with votre tête and poitrine up. Drive through the ground with your heels, extending your genous and hanches to raise the poids from the ground.
3. As you lean back, attempt to swing the poids onto the stairs, which are usually around 16-18" high. You can use vos jambes to help push the poids onto the stair.
4. Répétez for 3-5 repetitions, and continue with a heavier poids, moving as fast as possible.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Power_Stairs/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Preacher Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre', '1. To perform this movement you will need a preacher banc and an E-Z bar. Grab the E-Z curl bar at the close inner handle (either have someone hand you the bar which is preferable or grab the bar from the front bar rest provided by most preacher benches). The palm of vos mains should be facing forward and they should be slightly tilted inwards due to the shape of the bar.
2. With the upper arms positioned against the preacher banc pad and the poitrine against it, hold the E-Z Curl Bar at épaule length. C''est votre position de départ.
3. As you Inspirez, Lentement, lower the bar until your upper arm is extended and the biceps is fully stretched.
4. As you expirez, use the biceps to curl the poids up until your biceps is entièrement contracté and the bar is at épaule height. Squeeze the biceps hard and hold this position for a second.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Preacher_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Preacher Hammer Dumbbell Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Place the upper part of both arms on top of the preacher banc as you hold a haltère in each hand with the paumes vers each other (neutral grip).
2. As you Inspirez, Lentement, lower the haltères until your upper arm is extended and the biceps is fully stretched.
3. As you expirez, use the biceps to curl the poids up until your biceps is entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule height.
4. Squeeze the biceps hard for a second at the contracted position and Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Preacher_Hammer_Dumbbell_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Press Sit-Up', 'Abdominaux', 'Barre', '1. To begin, lie down on a banc with a barre resting on your poitrine. Position vos jambes so they are secure on the extension of the abdominal banc. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While inhaling, tighten your abdominals and fessiers. Simultaneously curl your torse as you do when performing a sit-up and press the barre to an overhead position while exhaling. Conseil : Use vos bras to push the barre out as you perform cet exercice while still focusing on the abdominal muscles.
3. Lower your upper body back down to the position de départ while bringing the barre back down to your torse. Remember to Inspirez while lowering the body.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Press_Sit-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Prone Manual Hamstring', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. You will need a partner for cet exercice. Lay face down with vos jambes straight. Your assistant will place their hand on your heel.
2. To begin, flex the genou to curl your leg up. Your partner should provide resistance, starting light and increasing the pressure as le mouvement is completed. Communicate with your partner to monitor appropriate resistance levels.
3. Pause at the top, returning the leg to the position de départ as your partner provides resistance going the other direction.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Prone_Manual_Hamstring/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Prowler Sprint', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Place your sled on an appropriate surface, loaded to a suitable poids. The sled should provide enough resistance to require effort, but not so heavy that you are significantly slowed down.
